.TH AD_REPLAY 1 "2026-09-10" "ad 2.0" "ad scripts"
.SH NAME
ad_replay \- replay a recorded animation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_replay
.RI <oldfile> " <recording.dv>"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_replay
replays a timed op stream previously recorded by
.BR ad_record (1).
It loads the old file into the animator as the initial buffer, then
feeds the timed op stream through
.B ad
(in
.B \-\-no\-display
mode at speed 1000, with
.BR \-\-snapshot )
so that the final buffer state is written to
.IR /tmp/ad_replay_out.txt .
.PP
This is the counterpart to
.BR ad_record :
the recording captures the timed ops, and this script replays them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show detailed help and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <oldfile>
Path to the original/source file used as the initial buffer (the same
file passed to
.BR ad_record ).
.TP
.I <recording.dv>
Path to a recording file produced by
.BR ad_record (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_replay old.py /tmp/my_recording.dv
Replay the recording, writing the final buffer to
.IR /tmp/ad_replay_out.txt .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ad_vim (1),
.BR ad_record (1),
.BR ad (1)
